# Testing

- Use JUnit 5 and Spring Boot Test (`spring-boot-starter-test`). Default integration smoke test uses `@SpringBootTest` and `@ActiveProfiles("test")`.
- H2 is available in the test scope; align `spring.datasource` / JPA settings in test resources with how the project already runs tests.
- For secured endpoints, use `spring-security-test` (`@WithMockUser`, `MockMvc`, etc.) following patterns consistent with existing tests when you add them.
- Prefer focused tests for new behavior (slice tests or `@WebMvcTest`) when they reduce flakiness and runtime; use full context only when necessary.
- CI runs `mvn -f pom.xml test` after `clean compile` — keep the test suite green before merging.
